# GaDeMa API Test Suite — REST Client Format (VS Code)

> **Protocol:** `HTTP/1.1` | **Base URL:** `https://localhost:5001/api/v1`  
> **Format:** RFC 2616-compliant with VS Code REST Client extension syntax

---

## 📋 Test Sequence: User Registration → Project Creation → Content Workflow

```http
### ===== STEP 1: REGISTER A NEW USER =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Connection: keep-alive
Cache-Control: no-cache

{
    "email": "developer@example.com",
    "password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!",
    "name": "Jane Developer"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 2: SIGN IN WITH REGISTERED CREDENTIALS =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/signin HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Connection: keep-alive

{
    "email": "developer@example.com",
    "password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 3: SIGN IN WITH GOOGLE OAUTH (ALTERNATIVE) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/callback/google HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

code=4/AO0aAm8Gf6r3XwQp2kL9mNvYzRtBcDsE&state=session-abc-123
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 4: SIGN IN WITH TWO-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/signin-with-2fa HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "email": "developer@example.com",
    "password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!",
    "twoFactorToken": "123456"  // Replace with actual TOTP token from authenticator app
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 5: CREATE A NEW PROJECT =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "title": "My RPG Adventure Game",
    "description": "A fantasy RPG with branching narrative and character progression.",
    "ownerType": 0,       // 0 = User-owned, 1 = Team-owned
    "visibility": "Private",  // Public | Private | TeamOnly
    "templateType": "RPG"   // Optional: use predefined project templates
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 6: LIST ALL PROJECTS (VERIFICATION) =====
GET https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects?pageSize=20&page=1 HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 7: CREATE A NEW CONTENT ITEM (Character) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content/items HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "projectId": "<PROJECT_ID_FROM_STEP_5>",
    "contentType": 0,         // ContentTypeEnum.Character = 0
    "title": "Elara Moonwhisper",
    "slug": "elara-moonwhisper",
    "shortDesc": "A rogue mage seeking redemption for her past.",
    "description": "# Character Sheet\n\n## Overview\n- **Name:** Elara Moonwhisper  \n- **Race:** Half-Elf  \n- **Class:** Arcane Rogue\n\n## Personality Traits\nElara carries a quiet determination in her eyes, haunted by the failure that led to her current quest. She speaks softly but with conviction.\n\n## Background\nFormer apprentice of the Sunspire Academy, she was expelled after discovering dark rituals within her mentor's teachings."
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 8: UPDATE THE CONTENT ITEM (Add Tags & Media) =====
PUT https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content/items/<CONTENT_ID_FROM_STEP_7> HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "description": "# Character Sheet\n\n## Overview\n- **Name:** Elara Moonwhisper  \n- **Race:** Half-Elf  \n- **Class:** Arcane Rogue  \n\n## Equipment\nWields a silver-tipped dagger and an ancient grimoire.\n\n## Abilities\n- *Shadow Step*: Teleport short distances in darkness.  \n- *Arcane Lockpicking*: Opens magical seals with a touch.",
    "published": false,
    "viewMode": "PrivateWriting",   // vs "Presentation" mode
    "tags": [
        "Protagonist",
        "MagicUser",
        "RogueClass",
        "HalfElf"
    ],
    "reviewStatusId": "<OPTIONAL_REVIEW_STATUS_ID>"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 9: CREATE A NEW STORY OUTLINE (Plot Point) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content/items HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "projectId": "<PROJECT_ID_FROM_STEP_5>",
    "contentType": 3,            // ContentTypeEnum.PlotPoint = 3
    "title": "The Fallen Kingdom",
    "slug": "the-fallen-kingdom",
    "shortDesc": "Act II climax where the kingdom is overtaken by corruption.",
    "description": "# Plot Point: The Fallen Kingdom\n\n## Synopsis\nThe dark forces Elara encountered in Act I have now consumed the entire kingdom of Aethelgard. The capital city lies in ruins, and survivors are scattered.\n\n## Beats\n- **Beat 1:** Elara arrives at the gates (destruction)\n- **Beat 2:** Discovery of the corrupted throne room\n- **Beat 3:** Confrontation with the corrupted king\n- **Beat 4:** The revelation that corruption spread through bloodlines, not just magic\n\n## Themes\nPower corrupts. Legacy. Sacrifice."
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 10: CREATE A DIALOGUE BRANCH (Visual Novel Style) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects/<PROJECT_ID>/dialogue/branches HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "projectId": "<PROJECT_ID_FROM_STEP_5>",
    "title": "Chapter 1: The Awakening",
    "visualNodeImageUri": "/assets/images/nodes/awakening_bg.png",
    "characterIconUri": "/assets/images/icons/elara_silverhair.png"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 11: ADD A DIALOGUE NODE TO THE BRANCH (Child Node) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects/<PROJECT_ID>/dialogue/branches/<BRANCH_ID>/nodes HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "branchId": "<BRANCH_ID_FROM_STEP_10>",
    "title": "The Stranger Approaches",
    "speakerName": "Unknown Traveler",
    "speakerRole": 0,            // 0 = Protagonist, 1 = NPC, 2 = Antagonist
    "dialogueText": "\"You're... the one they called the Moonwhisper.\"",
    "choices": [
        {
            "id": "choice_a",
            "label": "Introduce yourself.",
            "nextNodeId": "<CHILD_NODE_ID>",
            "conditions": {
                "requiredTraits": ["Polite"]
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "choice_b",
            "label": "Stay silent and watch.",
            "nextNodeId": "<CHILD_NODE_ID_ALT>",
            "conditions": {
                "requiredTraits": ["Cautious"]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 12: CREATE A PROJECT TASK (ADHD-Friendly Flat Structure) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/tasks HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "projectId": "<PROJECT_ID_FROM_STEP_5>",
    "contentItemId": null,       // null = project-level task, not tied to specific content
    "taskTitle": "Design the main character's ability tree",
    "description": "Create a complete skill/ability progression for Elara including:\n- Passive abilities (shadow step, smoke screen)\n- Active combat abilities\n- Utility abilities (lockpicking, stealth)",
    "status": 0,                 // TaskStatusEnum.Pending = 0, InProgress=1, Completed=2
    "priority": 1,              // 1 = Highest priority
    "difficulty": 2,            // 0 = Easy, 1 = Medium, 2 = Hard
    "isQuickWin": true,         // ✅ ADHD-friendly flag for quick wins
    "estimatedMinutes": 45,
    "assignedToUserId": null,   // Optional: leave null for unassigned
    "dueDate": "2025-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 13: ADD A COMMENT TO THE TASK (Team Collaboration) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/tasks/<TASK_ID_FROM_STEP_12>/comments HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "contentItemId": "<CONTENT_ID_FROM_STEP_7>",
    "text": "@developer Please review the ability tree before we start implementation. I want to make sure the passive abilities don't stack with each other.",
    "visibility": "Team"         // Private | Team | Public
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 14: SUBMIT CONTENT FOR REVIEW (Approval Workflow) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content-items/<CONTENT_ID_FROM_STEP_7>/review HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "status": 1,                 // ReviewStatusEnum.Pending = 1
    "assignedReviewerId": "<TEAM_MEMBER_ID>"
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 15: APPROVE CONTENT (Second User's Perspective) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content-items/<CONTENT_ID_FROM_STEP_7>/review HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <TEAM_MEMBER_ACCESS_TOKEN>

{
    "status": 2,                 // ReviewStatusEnum.Approved = 2
    "reviewerNotes": "Approved. The ability interactions are balanced."
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 16: EXTERNAL REFERENCE (Google Docs / Pinterest) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/content-items/<CONTENT_ID_FROM_STEP_7>/external-references HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "name": "Character Design Inspiration",
    "url": "https://www.pinterest.com/pin/123456789/",
    "sourceType": 0,             // 0 = Pinterest, 1 = GoogleDocs, 2 = ArtStation
    "thumbnailUrl": null         // Optional: auto-generated thumbnail from URL
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 17: EXPORT CONTENT AS JSON (For Unity/Unreal Import) =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/export/content/json HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "projectId": "<PROJECT_ID>",
    "includeRelationships": true,
    "version": 1
}
```

---

```http
### ===== STEP 18: SEARCH ACROSS ALL CONTENT (Full-Text) =====
GET https://localhost:5001/api/v1/search/content?q=moonwhisper&contentType=Character&status=Draft HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

```

---

## 📋 Expected Response Codes Reference

| Step | Endpoint | Expected Status | Description |
|------|----------|-----------------|-------------|
| 1 | POST /auth/register | `201 Created` | User created successfully |
| 2 | POST /auth/signin | `200 OK` + JWT token in body | Authentication successful |
| 3 | POST /auth/callback/google | `200 OK` + JWT token | OAuth flow complete |
| 4 | POST /auth/signin-with-2fa | `200 OK` + JWT token | 2FA verified, session active |
| 5 | POST /projects | `201 Created` | Project created with UUID |
| 6 | GET /projects?pageSize=20 | `200 OK` + pagination metadata | List of user's projects |
| 7 | POST /content/items | `201 Created` | Content item created (auto-assigns ID) |
| 8 | PUT /content-items/{id} | `200 OK` | Item updated, version incremented |
| 9 | POST /content/items | `201 Created` | Plot point created |
| 10 | POST /projects/{id}/dialogue/branches | `201 Created` | Branch tree root node created |
| 11 | POST /dialogue/branches/{id}/nodes | `201 Created` | Child dialogue node added |
| 12 | POST /tasks | `201 Created` | Flat task created (ADHD-friendly) |
| 13 | POST /tasks/{id}/comments | `201 Created` | Comment threaded to task |
| 14 | POST /content-items/{id}/review | `200 OK` | Review submitted for approval |
| 15 | POST /content-items/{id}/review | `200 OK` | Reviewer approves content |
| 16 | POST /content-items/{id}/external-references | `201 Created` | External link stored |
| 17 | POST /export/content/json | `200 OK` + JSON payload | Downloadable export |
| 18 | GET /search/content?q=... | `200 OK` + search results | Full-text search across domain |

---

## 🧪 VS Code REST Client Tips

**To use these in VS Code:**

1. Install the **REST Client** extension (Huachao Mao)
2. Save all requests above as a single `.http` file, e.g., `tests/api-test-sequence.http`
3. Run with: `Ctrl+Alt+N` or click "▶ Send Request" in the editor
4. Responses appear below each request automatically

**Pro tip — add response validation comments:**

```http
### ===== STEP 1: REGISTER A NEW USER =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "developer@example.com",
    "password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!",
    "name": "Jane Developer"
}

## @response validate status-code 201 && response.json().message === "User registered successfully"
```

---

This sequence exercises every major domain in the system: authentication, project lifecycle, content CRUD, versioning, dialogue trees, task management, review workflows, external references, and export. Each step builds on the previous one to simulate a real user workflow.